{
    "background_story": "Elsie was a free-spirited traveler who had a passion for exploring the world's most remote destinations. After saving up for years, she finally bought a minibus, which she lovingly named 'Bertha'. Elsie spent months converting Bertha into a cozy home on wheels, complete with a kitchenette, bunk beds, and a colorful paint job. With Bertha by her side, Elsie embarked on a series of epic road trips, driving through the rugged landscapes of New Zealand, the scenic coastlines of Australia, and the majestic mountains of South America. Along the way, she met fellow travelers, shared stories, and formed lasting bonds. Bertha, the trusty minibus, became a symbol of Elsie's independence and sense of adventure, ferrying her to some of the most breathtaking places on earth.",
